window.docContents[245].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.PqxdhCorrectModel/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___PqxdhCorrectModel":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E › PqxdhCorrectModel.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 3 headline theorems depend on it 270 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (14)def keyPairOfdef u32def pqxdhSpqrSessiondef pqxdhSessionParamsdef initiatorRecordExtrasdef initiateInputdef initiateStatestructure ResponderPreKeySecretsstructure PreKeyMessageFieldsdef PreKeyMessageFields.bytesdef responderRecordExtrasdef acceptInputdef recvPrekeyStatedef PreKeyBundleFields.signaturesVerify\n\n\n\nPQXDH Handshake Session Models (initiateState, recvPrekeyState)Trusted: the statement. Composes the pure PQXDH key-agreement specification (SignalPqxdh.Model.initiateKeys / acceptKeys) with initializeInitiatorSession / initializeRecipientSession and V1 SPQR (pqxdhSpqrSession) to model Alice's init and Bob's pre-key recv (process_prekey_bundle / process_prekey). See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md and Computational/docs/DEVIATIONS.md (DEV-PQ5, DEV-PQ6, DEV-PQ8).\n\n\n\nKeys\n\ndef keyPairOfL39–46 ↗#The key pair of 32 private-key bytes as libsignal makes it (PrivateKey::deserialize clamps; KeyPair::try_from / IdentityKeyPair::try_from derive the public key from the clamped scalar). This is the body of the session model's KeyPair.generate (LibsignalSession.lean), which takes its 32 bytes as BitVec 256 coins (keyToBytesVec32 coins) rather than as a byte vector; it is restated here on bytes so that no byte/word round trip enters the statement.\n\ndef u32L48–49 ↗#A model UInt32 from a 32-bit word.\n\nSPQR V1 session parameters (pqxdhSpqrSession, pqxdhSessionParams)\n\ndef pqxdhSpqrSessionL53–57 ↗#The V1 Spqr Bytes Bytes session instance for W: LibsignalSpqrV1.spqrV1Session W.C.F W.Q.K (= (LibsignalSpqrV1.spqrV1 W.C.F W.Q.K).spqrWith (spqrV1Init W.C.F W.Q.K) by rfl).\n\ndef pqxdhSessionParamsL59–64 ↗#The session-model parameters for PQXDH sessions (spqrOffSessionParams W.C with V1 SPQR pqxdhSpqrSession W replacing spqrOffB; spqrOffSessionParams W.C stays untouched for the SPQR-off statements, SmDir.lean).\n\nAlice's init\n\ndef initiatorRecordExtrasL68–82 ↗#Alice's record extras after init (process_prekey_bundle):* pending: one-time pre-key id (if any), signed pre-key id, Alice's base key base, timestamp 0 (DEV-PQ8);* kyber: the Kyber pre-key id and the serialized ciphertext 0x08 ‖ ct (set_kyber_ciphertext, set_unacknowledged_kyber_pre_key_id);* the registration ids: me's local id and the bundle's remote id;* alice_base_key: Alice's own base key, serialized.\n\ndef initiateInputL84–108 ↗#The model's input to Model.initiateKeys for me, bundle b and tape t:* Alice's identity key pair is me.idPriv's;* the base key's scalar is tape bytes 0..32 (KeyPair::generate, which clamps; so does x25519);* the Kyber coins are initiateKemCoins t (DEV-PQ6);* the peer is trusted (DEV-PQ5).Kyber keys are raw (1568 bytes, no type byte), as in the model.\n\ndef initiateStateL110–132 ↗#Alice's state after init in the model, for party P, identity me, bundle b and tape t, with the record extras it is encoded under (none: null):1. Model.initiateKeys gives the handshake keys (rk, ck, pqr) and header (else null);2. initializeInitiatorSession uses V1 SPQR (pqxdhSpqrSession W), Alice's and the peer's identity keys, the peer's signed pre-key as their ratchet key, and the ratchet key from tape bytes 160..192 (else null: all-zero DH);3. setUnacknowledgedPreKeyMessage.The ghost epochs are those of Params.initA (epoch 0, one receiver chain of epoch 0); they are not encoded.\n\nBob's pre-key recv\n\nstructure ResponderPreKeySecretsL136–150 ↗#Bob's pre-key material: the pre-keys a pre-key message names, from Bob's stores (preKeysNamedBy, SignalSession/PqDir.lean).\n\nstructure PreKeyMessageFieldsL152–170 ↗#A PQXDH pre-key message (message version 4, with a Kyber payload). The inner SignalMessage is arbitrary bytes.\n\ndef PreKeyMessageFields.bytesL172–181 ↗#The wire bytes of a pre-key message, as PreKeySignalMessage::new writes them: versionByte 4 ‖ protobuf { pre_key_id?, base_key, identity_key, message, registration_id, signed_pre_key_id, kyber_pre_key_id, kyber_ciphertext }.\n\ndef responderRecordExtrasL183–193 ↗#Bob's record extras after his pre-key recv (process_prekey): no pending pre-key (the session model's flag is clear after the successful decryption, so pending / kyber are not written), local registration id me's, remote id the message's, alice_base_key the message's base key, serialized.\n\ndef acceptInputL195–221 ↗#The model's input to Model.acceptKeys for me, keys k and message m. Bob's identity and pre-key pairs are derived as libsignal derives them (keyPairOf). The one-time pre-key is k's iff m names its id (otherwise none, and acceptKeys rejects a named but missing key). Trusted peer (DEV-PQ5), no replay refusal (DEV-PQ8).\n\ndef recvPrekeyStateL223–255 ↗#Bob's state after his pre-key recv in the model, for party P, identity me, keys k, message m, an empty record, and Bob's ratchet coins rc, with its record extras and the plaintext (none: abort; some none: null). Each step's failure gives null:1. the inner message parses (SignalMessage.tryFrom);2. m's signed and Kyber pre-key ids are k's (get_signed_pre_key, get_kyber_pre_key);3. Model.acceptKeys gives (rk, ck, pqr);4. initializeRecipientSession with V1 SPQR (pqxdhSpqrSession W) and the signed pre-key pair as Bob's ratchet key;5. tryDecryptFromRecord (type PreKey, the addresses P expects, coins rc) gives the plaintext. A panic aborts.The ghost epochs are those Params.receive gives from Params.initB on a first message (epoch 1, one receiver chain of epoch 1); they are not encoded.\n\nThe bundle's signatures\n\ndef PreKeyBundleFields.signaturesVerifyL259–271 ↗#The bundle's two signatures verify, exactly as Model.initiateKeys checks them (the model's sigVerify, i.e. xeddsaVerifyRef at modelPrims): the signed pre-key's signature on 0x05 ‖ spk_pub and the Kyber pre-key's on 0x08 ‖ kpk_pub, both under id_pub (process_prekey_bundle, rust/protocol/src/session.rs).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E/PqxdhCorrectModel.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.PqxdhCorrectModel/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___PqxdhCorrectModel"},"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Misc/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Misc":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls › Misc.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 7 of 41 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nThread Identity and Affinity SyscallsTrusted syscall dispatch bundle (Syscall.miscTable, Syscall.misc) re-exporting Kernel.Sys for single-thread set_tid_address, sched_getaffinity, getpid, and gettid.\n\n\n\ndef miscTableL28–42 ↗#Dispatch table for single-thread identity and CPU-affinity syscalls (set_tid_address, sched_getaffinity, getpid, gettid).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 36–37): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Syscall.misc\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Misc.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Misc/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Misc"}});